            <ArticleTitle>Pain in the distribution of the femoral nerve: early evidence of recurrence of a retroperitoneal sarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>692-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain in the distribution of the femoral nerve following resection of a retroperitoneal sarcoma may signify tumor recurrence and should require exploration of the nerve to its origin from the spine in order to rule out a small, undetectable recurrence by CT scan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
